
Canny Edge Detection - data partitioning (CEDD)

Fetch the dataset (from the repository root)

    dvc pull src/data/ced/input.dvc src/data/ced/output.dvc

The frames are not hosted by HeCBench: src/data/ced/*.dvc are `dvc import`s
of CUDA-D/CEDD/{input,output} from the Chai repository
(https://github.com/chai-benchmarks/chai, pinned commit 61db988), shared by
ced-cuda, ced-hip and ced-sycl.

Compilation instructions:

    make

Execution instructions

    ./cedd

For more options:

    ./cedd -h


Note:
The input folder contains frames from a sample video. In order to generate frames 
with a format suitable for this benchmark, use utils/convert_frames in the Chai repository.
The output folder contains output frames for comparison purposes. In order to 
generate output frames, use utils/ced_output_frames in the Chai repository.

Acknowledgements:
Sean Kelley (https://github.com/smskelley/canny-opencl)

Read more:
J. Canny, “A computational approach to edge detection,” Pattern Analysis and 
Machine Intelligence, IEEE Transactions on, no. 6, pp. 679–698, 1986.
